A||N||7||Haze_Performance||I gotta Charging question.....||||10||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||11-25-2000||03:10 AM||||I replaced the Alt. in my 87 SE. When the car is started the Volt light stays on. If i rev the engine the light will slightly dim for a sec. A few days ago I started the car and parked it out side to warm up. All seemed fine untill the car started bogging and died. I tried to restart it but the battery was now dead. I thought that the battery might be bad to start with so I bought a new one. The Volt light is still on when I start the car... Is there something I can look for to see if I have a bad ground or something? I wouldnt enjoy pulling the Alt. back out to have it tested if I didnt have too.<P><BR>TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B>||||reg||10
Z||000001||robertjay||11-25-2000||09:51 AM||||I had the same problem after replacing mine, it turned out it was a broken bottom mounting bolt on the alternator.  I must have overtightened it.  But it would only spin the pulley fast enough to just turn the light out.  Never had a problem with it  overheating either......funny.<P>I have also had a pulley come loose on me after purchasing an alternator at Shuck's, They used an electric impact to swap the pulley, and it must not have been enough.<P>Good Luck!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||11-25-2000||12:43 PM||||Thanks robertjay.. The bolts are good and the pulley is tight. Plus I used a new belt    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Anyone else? <P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">    <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 11-25-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||maninblack||11-25-2000||02:13 PM||||maybe check the return cable from the alt. to the battery.or relace it,should be quite cheap frm your local parts store.It sounds like your alt. was unable to recharge you battery||||reg||1
Z||000004||strdream||11-25-2000||02:33 PM||||Haze   <BR>  Did the problem start at the same time you put the mew alt in?  If so,  It makes me think it is in the alt.  The symptoms you describe point to a faulty diode.  First I would check the connections on the terminals on the alt.  You didn't happen to put on what I call a self exciting alt. on did you?  If so  the light on the dash won't work right.  Put a volt meter on the alt lug, start the engine, rev it up good once and test the output. If you get right around 14v at the alt. than you are going to have to do something else to turn the light off.<P>We can get into that later if we need to.<P>Ross   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||strdream||11-25-2000||02:38 PM||||Haze   <BR>  Did the problem start at the same time you put the new alt in?  If so,  It makes me think it is in the alt.  The symptoms you describe point to a faulty diode.  First I would check the connections on the terminals on the alt.  You didn't happen to put on what I call a self exciting alt. on did you?  If so  the light on the dash won't work right.  Put a volt meter on the alt lug, start the engine, rev it up good once and test the output. If you get right around 14v at the alt. than you are going to have to do something else to turn the light off.<P>We can get into that later if we need to.<P>Ross   ||||reg||1
Z||000006||strdream||11-25-2000||02:39 PM||||OOPS!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||11-25-2000||09:58 PM||||Check and make sure you have the 12V at the alternator lug (car not running) If it is not 12V then the fuse link in the wire is bad. (running it should have 14.4V) If the old alt shorted out it could have blown the fuse link. Make sure you replace link with same gage link. It should be located near the battery junction block. Your volt gage should show about 14.4V. If gage isn't working and volt light is on there is a diode in the brown wire behind the gage assembly.  If it is bad the battery will still charge but gage/light won't work.<BR>If you have a Haynes Manual look on page 280 for the schematic.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
